LATENT DISPATCH
Wed Sep 16 · 5 items · ~4 min

SABLE-3.1: A POINT RELEASE THAT MATTERS
Better instruction following, fewer refusals on benign enterprise content, and a fix for the long-context recall cliff we flagged in August. Same price. If you are on Sable-3, upgrade; if you pinned a version, re-run your regression set first. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/sable-31

SHOULD THE ROUTING LAYER BE A PRODUCT?
With four providers matching each other's prices weekly, the value of a smart router that picks the cheapest model meeting a quality bar is obvious. Three startups are selling exactly that. The counter-argument: a router is 200 lines of code and a config file, and owning it means owning your fallback behavior. We lean toward build. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/routing-layer

FERRITE-70B NOW ON ARGENT
$0.55 / $1.70 per million, five cents under Kestrel. The open-model price war has begun.

MARROW SPEECH ADDS REAL-TIME
Sub-second streaming transcription with the same noise robustness. Useful for anyone building voice on the shop floor.

SHORT TAKES
· Lodestone publishes an "R2 in production" guide with recommended reasoning caps per task type.
· Pelagic 2.5 gets prompt caching. All five major labs now have it.
